STAT:9902296.canonicalSolution:
Areas: \(A_1=A_3=960\,\mathrm{mm}^2\), \(A_2=1152\,\mathrm{mm}^2\), \(A=3072\,\mathrm{mm}^2\). Own-centroid locations: bottom \((40,6)\), web \((74,60)\), top \((108,114)\,\mathrm{mm}\).
\[
\bar{x}=\frac{960(40)+1152(74)+960(108)}{3072}=74\,\mathrm{mm},\qquad
\bar{y}=\frac{960(6)+1152(60)+960(114)}{3072}=60\,\mathrm{mm}.
\]
Offsets: bottom \((\Delta x,\Delta y)=(-34,-54)\,\mathrm{mm}\); web \((0,0)\); top \((+34,+54)\,\mathrm{mm}\). Sides are parallel to the axes, so each rectangle has vanishing *own* product of inertia.
\[
\begin{align*}
I_{\bar{x}}
&=2\left[\frac{80\cdot 12^3}{12}+960(54)^2\right]+\frac{12\cdot 96^3}{12}
=6.506\times 10^6\,\mathrm{mm}^4,\\[4pt]
I_{\bar{y}}
&=2\left[\frac{12\cdot 80^3}{12}+960(34)^2\right]+\frac{96\cdot 12^3}{12}
=3.257\times 10^6\,\mathrm{mm}^4,\\[4pt]
I_{\bar{x}\bar{y}}
&=2\bigl[960(-34)(-54)\bigr]+0
=3.525\times 10^6\,\mathrm{mm}^4.
\end{align*}
\]
The two flanges are congruent and placed symmetrically with respect to the web centre, so the section centroid is exactly the web centroid and \(I_{\bar{x}\bar{y}}\) is twice the flange contribution and is *positive*. So \(I_{\bar{x}}=6.51\times 10^6\,\mathrm{mm}^4\), \(I_{\bar{y}}=3.26\times 10^6\,\mathrm{mm}^4\), \(I_{\bar{x}\bar{y}}=3.53\times 10^6\,\mathrm{mm}^4\).

