HEAT:9906245.canonicalSolution:
Product of two plane walls uses the half-thicknesses 20 mm and 9 mm. At 90 s, \(Fo_x=\alpha t/L_x^2=0.194<0.2\), so the second \(x\)-eigenvalue is retained. Results:
90 s: \(T_c=301^\circ\mathrm{C}\), \(T_{40}=413^\circ\mathrm{C}\), \(T_{18}=481^\circ\mathrm{C}\), \(T_{\mathrm{cor}}=545^\circ\mathrm{C}\);
240 s: \(593,627,651,669^\circ\mathrm{C}\);
\(q''(18\,\mathrm{mm\,mid},90\,\mathrm{s})=h(T_\infty-T_s)=44.2\,\mathrm{kW/m^2}\);
center exceeds 500 °C at \(t=172\,\mathrm{s}\).

### Final answer

90 s: \(T_c=301^\circ\mathrm{C}\), \(T_{40}=413^\circ\mathrm{C}\), \(T_{18}=481^\circ\mathrm{C}\), \(T_{\mathrm{cor}}=545^\circ\mathrm{C}\) (two \(x\)-terms); 240 s: \(593,627,651,669^\circ\mathrm{C}\); \(q''(18\,\mathrm{mm\,mid},90\,\mathrm{s})=44.2\,\mathrm{kW/m^2}\); \(t_{500}=172\,\mathrm{s}\).

