APAB:9913024.canonicalSolution:
For \(x\neq 0\),
\[
\sqrt{9x^2+4}=\sqrt{x^2\bigl(9+4/x^2\bigr)}=|x|\sqrt{9+4/x^2}.
\]
As \(x\to+\infty\), one has \(|x|=x\), so
\[
\frac{\sqrt{9x^2+4}}{2x-5}
=\frac{x\sqrt{9+4/x^2}}{x\bigl(2-5/x\bigr)}
=\frac{\sqrt{9+4/x^2}}{2-5/x}
\to\frac{3}{2}.
\]
As \(x\to-\infty\), one has \(|x|=-x\), so
\[
\frac{\sqrt{9x^2+4}}{2x-5}
=\frac{-x\sqrt{9+4/x^2}}{x\bigl(2-5/x\bigr)}
=\frac{-\sqrt{9+4/x^2}}{2-5/x}
\to\frac{-3}{2}.
\]

**Final answer.** \(3/2\) and \(-3/2\)

