For \(x\neq 0\),
\[
\sqrt{4x^2+1}=\sqrt{x^2\bigl(4+1/x^2\bigr)}=|x|\sqrt{4+1/x^2}.
\]
As \(x\to+\infty\), one has \(|x|=x\), so
\[
\frac{\sqrt{4x^2+1}}{x-3}
=\frac{x\sqrt{4+1/x^2}}{x\bigl(1-3/x\bigr)}
=\frac{\sqrt{4+1/x^2}}{1-3/x}
\to\frac{2}{1}=2.
\]
As \(x\to-\infty\), one has \(|x|=-x\), so
\[
