DLOG:9918031.statement:
A combinational network has inputs \(A\), \(B\), \(C\) and a single output \(F\). Internal nodes are defined as follows:
- \(P=\overline{AB}\) (2-input NAND of \(A\) and \(B\));
- \(Q=B\oplus C\) (2-input XOR of \(B\) and \(C\));
- \(R=\overline{P+C}\) (2-input NOR of \(P\) and \(C\));
- \(F=Q\cdot\overline{R}\) (2-input AND of \(Q\) with the complement of \(R\)).

Using the variable order \(ABC\) with \(A\) most significant, construct the 8-row truth table of \(F\) for \(ABC=000,001,\ldots,111\). Write \(F\) as a sum of minterms in decimal index form \(\sum m(\ldots)\).

DLOG:9918070.statement:
An 8-bit two's-complement adder/subtractor computes \(R=A+B\) when \(M=0\) and \(R=A+\overline{B}+1\) when \(M=1\), using a single 8-bit ripple adder whose carry-in is \(M\) and whose \(B\) inputs are exclusive-ORed with \(M\). Bit \(7\) is the MSB. Flags are defined from the adder as follows:
- \(N=r_7\);
- \(Z=1\) iff \(R=00000000\);
- \(C\) is the carry-out \(C_8\) of the adder;
- \(V=C_8\oplus C_7\), where \(C_7\) is the carry into the MSB full adder.

Let \(A=01011100\) and \(B=10100011\).

(a) For \(M=0\), compute the adder operands, every carry \(C_1,\ldots,C_8\), the result \(R\), and the flags \(N,Z,C,V\). Interpret \(A\), \(B\), and \(R\) as unsigned integers and as two's-complement integers, and state whether each interpretation of \(R\) is arithmetically correct in 8 bits.

(b) Repeat (a) for \(M=1\).

(c) Using only the definition \(V=C_8\oplus C_7\), show that \(V=1\) in (b) if and only if the two's-complement interpretation of \(A-B\) lies outside \(\{-128,\ldots,127\}\).

DLOG:9918082.statement:
A 1-bit ALU slice has data inputs \(A\), \(B\), and \(C_{\mathrm{in}}\), control inputs \(M\), \(S_1\), \(S_0\), and outputs \(R\) and \(C_{\mathrm{out}}\). Define \(B^*=B\oplus M\). The slice function is:
- \(S_1S_0=00\): \(R=AB^*\), \(C_{\mathrm{out}}=0\);
- \(S_1S_0=01\): \(R=A+B^*\) (OR), \(C_{\mathrm{out}}=0\);
- \(S_1S_0=10\): \(R=A\oplus B^*\), \(C_{\mathrm{out}}=0\);
- \(S_1S_0=11\): \(R=A\oplus B^*\oplus C_{\mathrm{in}}\), \(C_{\mathrm{out}}=AB^*+B^*C_{\mathrm{in}}+C_{\mathrm{in}}A\).

(a) Fill a table giving \(R\) and \(C_{\mathrm{out}}\) for every combination of \(S_1S_0\) with the fixed data \((A,B,C_{\mathrm{in}})=(1,0,1)\), once for \(M=0\) and once for \(M=1\). That is eight rows.

(b) Identify the control settings \((M,S_1,S_0,C_{\mathrm{in}})\) that realise, on this slice, the operations \(A\land B\), \(A\lor B\), \(A\oplus B\), \(A+B\) (binary addition, including carry), and \(A-B\) (two's-complement subtraction on this bit, including carry). For subtraction, state the required \(C_{\mathrm{in}}\) of the least-significant slice of a wider ALU.

(c) For \(A=1\), \(B=1\), \(M=1\), \(S_1S_0=11\), \(C_{\mathrm{in}}=1\), compute \(R\) and \(C_{\mathrm{out}}\) and interpret them as the LSB of a two's-complement subtraction of two odd integers.

DLOG:9918092.canonicalSolution:
The eight truth-table rows of \(F\) are \(1\) precisely on minterms \(0,2,3,5\):
\[
\begin{array}{c|cccccccc}
ABC & 000 & 001 & 010 & 011 & 100 & 101 & 110 & 111\\
F & 1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 0
\end{array}
\]

(a) Pair rows that share a fixed \(AB\) and vary \(C\):

- \(AB=00\): \((C,F)=(0,1),(1,0)\), so \(F|_{AB=00}=\overline{C}\) and \(I_0=\overline{C}\);
- \(AB=01\): both rows are \(1\), so \(F|_{AB=01}=1\) and \(I_1=1\);
- \(AB=10\): \((C,F)=(0,0),(1,1)\), so \(F|_{AB=10}=C\) and \(I_2=C\);
- \(AB=11\): both rows are \(0\), so \(F|_{AB=11}=0\) and \(I_3=0\).

Among \(\{0,1,C,\overline{C}\}\) each cofactor is unique, so the assignment \(I_0=\overline{C}\), \(I_1=1\), \(I_2=C\), \(I_3=0\) is unique.

(b) Substitute:
\[
Y=\overline{A}\,\overline{B}\,\overline{C}+\overline{A}B\cdot 1+A\overline{B}C+AB\cdot 0
=\overline{A}\,\overline{B}\,\overline{C}+\overline{A}B+A\overline{B}C.
\]
The middle term expands as \(\overline{A}B=\overline{A}B\overline{C}+\overline{A}BC=m_2+m_3\), while \(\overline{A}\,\overline{B}\,\overline{C}=m_0\) and \(A\overline{B}C=m_5\). The on-set is \(\{0,2,3,5\}\), matching the specification.

(c) Now pair rows that share a fixed \(BC\) and vary \(A\):

- \(BC=00\): \(A=0\) gives \(m_0=1\), \(A=1\) gives \(m_4=0\), so \(I_0=\overline{A}\);
- \(BC=01\): \(m_1=0\), \(m_5=1\), so \(I_1=A\);
- \(BC=10\): \(m_2=1\), \(m_6=0\), so \(I_2=\overline{A}\);
- \(BC=11\): \(m_3=1\), \(m_7=0\), so \(I_3=\overline{A}\).

**Answers.** (a) \(\overline{C}\), \(1\), \(C\), \(0\); \(I_0=\overline{C}\), \(I_1=1\), \(I_2=C\), \(I_3=0\). (b) \(\sum m(0,2,3,5)\), matches. (c) \(I_0=\overline{A}\), \(I_1=A\), \(I_2=\overline{A}\), \(I_3=\overline{A}\).

