DLOG:9918112.canonicalSolution:
Fix \(AB\) and read the residual in \(C\).

(a) Majority:

- \(AB=00\): \(M=0\), so \(I_0=0\);
- \(AB=01\): \(M=C\), so \(I_1=C\);
- \(AB=10\): \(M=C\), so \(I_2=C\);
- \(AB=11\): \(M=1\), so \(I_3=1\).

Unique in \(\{0,1,C,\overline{C}\}\): \(I_0=0\), \(I_1=C\), \(I_2=C\), \(I_3=1\).

(b) Three-input XOR:

- \(AB=00\): \(S=C\), so \(I_0=C\);
- \(AB=01\): \(S=\overline{C}\), so \(I_1=\overline{C}\);
- \(AB=10\): \(S=\overline{C}\), so \(I_2=\overline{C}\);
- \(AB=11\): \(S=C\), so \(I_3=C\).

Unique: \(I_0=C\), \(I_1=\overline{C}\), \(I_2=\overline{C}\), \(I_3=C\).

(c) Full adder: \(1+1+0=10_2\), so at \(ABC=110\) one has \((S,C_{\mathrm{out}})=(0,1)\). And \(0+1+1=10_2\), so at \(ABC=011\) again \((S,C_{\mathrm{out}})=(0,1)\). Directly: \(M(1,1,0)=1\), \(S(1,1,0)=0\); \(M(0,1,1)=1\), \(S(0,1,1)=0\).

(d) Assignment (a) uses only \(0,1,C\). Assignment (b) uses \(\overline{C}\) on two pins (\(I_1\) and \(I_2\) of the XOR mux). Two data pins require the inverted literal; one shared inverter serves both.

**Answers.** (a) \(0,C,C,1\). (b) \(C,\overline{C},\overline{C},C\). (c) \((0,1)\) at both points. (d) \(2\) pins.

