ALG:9920031.canonicalSolution:
For an empty array, report absence. Otherwise:

```text
lo = 0
hi = n - 1
while lo <= hi:
    mid = lo + floor((hi - lo) / 2)
    if A[mid] == x:
        return mid

    if A[lo] <= A[mid]:
        if A[lo] <= x and x < A[mid]:
            hi = mid - 1
        else:
            lo = mid + 1
    else:
        if A[mid] < x and x <= A[hi]:
            lo = mid + 1
        else:
            hi = mid - 1
report absent
```

Maintain: if \(x\) occurs, its index is in \([\texttt{lo},\texttt{hi}]\). A rotated strictly increasing array has at most one descent, so at least one side of the midpoint is sorted. If the left side is sorted, it contains \(x\) exactly when
\[
A[\texttt{lo}]\le x<A[\texttt{mid}],
\]
because midpoint equality was already tested. The update keeps that side exactly in this case. The right-side argument is symmetric. Hence the invariant is preserved.

The interval strictly shrinks and is at least halved. Finding equality is correct, while an empty interval proves absence by the invariant. Time is \(O(\log n)\), and the iterative implementation uses \(O(1)\) auxiliary space.

