Substitute \(z=-3\):
\begin{align*}
R(-3)
&=1+(-3)+\frac{(-3)^2}{2}+\frac{(-3)^3}{6}+\frac{(-3)^4}{24}\\
&=1-3+\frac{9}{2}-\frac{27}{6}+\frac{81}{24}\\
&=-2+\frac{9}{2}-\frac{9}{2}+\frac{27}{8}
=\frac{-16}{8}+\frac{27}{8}
=\frac{11}{8}.
\end{align*}
Thus \(|R(-3)|=11/8>1\). Therefore \(z=-3\) does **not** lie in the region of absolute stability.

**Final answer.** \(|R(-3)|=11/8>1\); \(z=-3\notin\mathcal{S}\).

