ARCH:9923080.canonicalSolution:
`0x8D2A0004` \(=\) `1000 1101 0010 1010 0000 0000 0000 0100`, so

\[
\begin{align*}
\mathrm{opcode}[31:26]&=100011,\\
\mathrm{rs}[25:21]&=01001=9,\\
\mathrm{rt}[20:16]&=01010=10,\\
\mathrm{imm}[15:0]&=\mathtt{0x0004}.
\end{align*}
\]

Opcode \(100011\) is LW. From the table of Problem 75:

\[
\mathrm{RegDst}=0,\;
\mathrm{ALUSrc}=1,\;
\mathrm{MemtoReg}=1,\;
\mathrm{RegWrite}=1,\;
\mathrm{MemRead}=1,\;
\mathrm{MemWrite}=0,\;
\mathrm{Branch}=0,\;
\mathrm{ALUOp}=00.
\]

ALUOp \(=00\) forces add, and ALUSrc \(=1\) feeds the sign-extended immediate, so the data-memory address is

\[
R[9]+\mathtt{0x00000004}
=\mathtt{0x10000000}+\mathtt{0x00000004}
=\mathtt{0x10000004}.
\]

RegDst \(=0\) selects `rt`, RegWrite \(=1\), and MemtoReg \(=1\), so at the end of the cycle **register 10** is written from **data memory** (\(\mathrm{Mem}[\mathtt{0x10000004}]\)). Data memory itself is not written.

