ARCH:9923081.canonicalSolution:
Five class delays are listed (the authored “four” is a wording slip). A single-cycle clock must close every class, so the mix does not enter the period calculation:

\[
T_{\mathrm{clk}}
=\max\{680,900,710,640,400\}
=900\,\mathrm{ps},
\]

set by LW.

With \(\mathrm{CPI}=1\), average instruction execution time is

\[
\mathrm{CPI}\times T_{\mathrm{clk}}=900\,\mathrm{ps}.
\]

(The mix would matter only if different classes occupied different numbers of cycles.) Throughput is

\[
\frac{1}{T_{\mathrm{clk}}}
=\frac{1}{900\times 10^{-12}\,\mathrm{s}}
=\frac{10}{9}\times 10^{9}\,\mathrm{s}^{-1}
=\frac{10}{9}\,\mathrm{GIPS}
\approx 1.111\,\mathrm{GIPS}.
\]

