hintTree.content:
(i) Split each VA. (ii) Look up the PTE. (iii) Stop at the first failed C-check. (iv) On SUCCESS, concatenate PPN with offset.

### Solution

VPN \(=\mathrm{VA}[15:8]\), offset \(=\mathrm{VA}[7:0]\), \(\mathrm{PA}=\mathrm{PPN}\mathbin{\Vert}\mathrm{offset}\). Decode the low byte of each PTE as flags `DAXWURV`.

(1) VPN `0x10`, offset `0xA4`. PTE `0x5C07`: PPN `0x5C`, \(V=1\), \(U=1\), \(R=1\), \(W=0\), \(X=0\). C1–C2–C4 pass. PA `0x5CA4`.

(2) VPN `0x11`, offset `0xB0`. PTE `0x5D0D`: PPN `0x5D`, \(V=1\), \(U=1\), \(R=0\), \(W=1\), \(X=0\). Store uses C5, not C4; \(W=1\). PA `0x5DB0`.

(3) VPN `0x12`, offset `0x00`. PTE `0x5E05`: \(V=1\), \(U=1\), \(X=0\). C3 fails. Protection-violation.

(4) VPN `0x13`, offset `0xFC`. PTE `0x0000`: \(V=0\). C1 fails. Not-present.

(5) VPN `0x14`, offset `0x08`. PTE `0x6003`: PPN `0x60`, \(V=1\), \(U=0\), \(R=1\), \(W=0\). Kernel skips C2; C5 fails on \(W=0\). Protection-violation.

(6) VPN `0x15`, offset `0x00`. PTE `0x611F`: PPN `0x61`, \(V=1\), \(U=1\), \(R=1\), \(W=1\), \(X=1\). PA `0x6100`.

(7) VPN `0x11`, offset `0xC2`. Same PTE as (2): \(X=0\). Kernel skips C2; C3 fails. Protection-violation.

(8) VPN `0x10`, offset `0x40`. Same PTE as (1): \(W=0\). C5 fails. Protection-violation.

**Answers.**
(1) VPN `0x10`, offset `0xA4`, PA `0x5CA4`;
(2) VPN `0x11`, offset `0xB0`, PA `0x5DB0`;
(3) VPN `0x12`, offset `0x00`, protection-violation;
(4) VPN `0x13`, offset `0xFC`, not-present;
(5) VPN `0x14`, offset `0x08`, protection-violation;
(6) VPN `0x15`, offset `0x00`, PA `0x6100`;
(7) VPN `0x11`, offset `0xC2`, protection-violation;
(8) VPN `0x10`, offset `0x40`, protection-violation.

---

