ELEC:9924030.statement:
A student proposes an unregulated DC supply with the following written specification and bill of materials. The specification: “\(12\,\mathrm{V}\) DC nominal, \(200\,\mathrm{mA}\) maximum load, peak-to-peak ripple at most \(0.50\,\mathrm{V}\), \(60.0\,\mathrm{Hz}\) mains, bridge rectifier, capacitor-input filter, transformer secondary RMS \(9.00\,\mathrm{V}\).” The bill of materials: a transformer with secondary rating \(9.00\,\mathrm{V}\) RMS, \(0.500\,\mathrm{A}\); four \(1\,\mathrm{N}4001\) diodes (\(V_{\mathrm{RRM}}=50\,\mathrm{V}\), \(I_{F(\mathrm{AV})}=1.00\,\mathrm{A}\), \(I_{\mathrm{FSM}}=30.0\,\mathrm{A}\)); a single aluminum electrolytic \(C=1000\,\mu\mathrm{F}\) at \(16\,\mathrm{V}\); no surge resistor; no bleeder; load modeled as \(R_L=60.0\,\Omega\).

Use the constant-drop model with \(V_\gamma=0.850\,\mathrm{V}\) per diode (two drops in a conducting bridge path), the linear-ramp ripple formula \(\Delta V=V_p/(f_{\mathrm{ripple}} R_L C)\) with \(f_{\mathrm{ripple}}=120\,\mathrm{Hz}\) for a healthy bridge, and \(V_p=V_m-2V_\gamma\) with \(V_m=9.00\sqrt{2}\,\mathrm{V}\). Ignore transformer regulation, ESR, and temperature unless a listed part rating forces the issue. The downstream load must remain at least \(11.0\,\mathrm{V}\) at the ripple trough at \(200\,\mathrm{mA}\).

Audit the design. For each of the following items, compute the relevant quantity and issue a verdict of adequate, inadequate, or indeterminate-from-the-stated-model:

(a) no-load peak voltage versus the \(16\,\mathrm{V}\) capacitor rating;

(b) full-load average voltage and ripple trough versus the \(11.0\,\mathrm{V}\) trough requirement;

(c) ripple versus the \(0.50\,\mathrm{V}\) peak-to-peak specification;

(d) diode PIV versus \(V_{\mathrm{RRM}}\);

(e) diode average current versus \(I_{F(\mathrm{AV})}\);

(f) first-cycle inrush versus \(I_{\mathrm{FSM}}\), using the unbounded \(C\,dv/dt\) estimate of Problem 24(a) at the conduction threshold;

(g) transformer secondary RMS current versus the \(0.500\,\mathrm{A}\) rating, approximating the secondary current as a full-wave rectified sinusoid of peak \(V_p/R_L\).

Then list every specification failure in a single summary sentence, and state the smallest change to \(C\) alone that would meet the ripple specification (a) through (c) if all other verdicts are ignored. Do not introduce a linear regulator, and do not invoke a Zener that is not on the bill of materials.

ELEC:9924050.statement:
A zener datasheet excerpt for a single part, all entries at \(T_A=25^\circ\mathrm{C}\), reads:
- \(V_Z=5.60\,\mathrm{V}\) typical at \(I_{ZT}=20.0\,\mathrm{mA}\);
- \(I_{ZK}=1.00\,\mathrm{mA}\), with \(V_Z\) guaranteed only for \(i_Z\ge I_{ZK}\);
- \(Z_Z=8.00\,\Omega\) typical, defined as \(\Delta V_Z/\Delta I_Z\) about \(I_{ZT}\) with \(\Delta I_Z=\pm 0.10 I_{ZT}\);
- \(I_{ZM}=70.0\,\mathrm{mA}\), the current at which the dissipation rating is reached at \(V_Z=5.60\,\mathrm{V}\).

Adopt the local linear model \(v_Z=V_{Z}(I_{ZT})+Z_Z(i_Z-I_{ZT})\) for \(I_{ZK}\le i_Z\le I_{ZM}\), with \(v_Z\) the cathode-to-anode voltage and \(i_Z\) into the cathode. A shunt regulator is assembled as follows. An unregulated DC source \(V_{\mathrm{in}}=12.0\,\mathrm{V}\) has its negative terminal grounded. A resistor \(R_s=270\,\Omega\) joins the positive terminal of \(V_{\mathrm{in}}\) to the output node \(O\). This zener has its cathode at \(O\) and its anode at ground. A load \(R_L=680\,\Omega\) joins \(O\) to ground. The output is \(v_o=v_O\).

Solve for the operating point \((v_o,i_Z,i_L)\). Verify that \(i_Z\) lies in \([I_{ZK},I_{ZM}]\). Using \(Z_Z\) as \(r_z\), compute the small-signal line regulation \(\partial v_o/\partial V_{\mathrm{in}}\) at this operating point with \(R_L\) fixed. If a designer instead treats the zener as an ideal \(5.60\,\mathrm{V}\) source, compute the error in predicted \(v_o\) relative to the linear model.

ELEC:9924061.canonicalSolution:
Form \(v_{GS}=v_G-v_S\), \(v_{DS}=v_D-v_S\), \(v_{GD}=v_G-v_D\), and compare with \(V_{tn}=0.80\,\mathrm{V}\). No current is requested.

**(a)** \(v_{GS}=0.50\,\mathrm{V}\), \(v_{DS}=4.00\,\mathrm{V}\), \(v_{GD}=-3.50\,\mathrm{V}\).
Since \(v_{GS}=0.50\,\mathrm{V}<0.80\,\mathrm{V}\), the device is in **cutoff** and \(i_D=0\). (The large positive \(v_{DS}\) is irrelevant once the inversion test fails.)

**(b)** \(v_{GS}=2.20\,\mathrm{V}\), \(v_{DS}=0.50\,\mathrm{V}\), \(v_{GD}=1.70\,\mathrm{V}\).
Now \(v_{GS}=2.20\,\mathrm{V}\ge 0.80\,\mathrm{V}\) and \(v_{OV}=1.40\,\mathrm{V}\). Then \(v_{DS}=0.50\,\mathrm{V}<1.40\,\mathrm{V}\), equivalently \(v_{GD}=1.70\,\mathrm{V}>0.80\,\mathrm{V}\). The device is in **triode** and the triode current formula is required.

**(c)** \(v_{GS}=2.20\,\mathrm{V}\), \(v_{DS}=3.30\,\mathrm{V}\), \(v_{GD}=-1.10\,\mathrm{V}\).
Again \(v_{GS}\ge V_{tn}\) with \(v_{OV}=1.40\,\mathrm{V}\), but now \(v_{DS}=3.30\,\mathrm{V}\ge 1.40\,\mathrm{V}\), equivalently \(v_{GD}=-1.10\,\mathrm{V}\le 0.80\,\mathrm{V}\). The device is in **saturation** and the saturation current formula is required.

**(d)** \(v_{GS}=2.20\,\mathrm{V}\), \(v_{DS}=1.40\,\mathrm{V}\), \(v_{GD}=0.80\,\mathrm{V}\).
Here \(v_{DS}=v_{GS}-V_{tn}\) and \(v_{GD}=V_{tn}\) exactly: the **pinch-off boundary**. By the stated tests this point is included in saturation (\(v_{DS}\ge v_{OV}\), \(v_{GD}\le V_{tn}\)); the opening paragraph also permits a triode label. Either conducting-region formula may be used; they agree.

**(e)** Saturation, including the boundary in the sense of the listed tests, is the conjunction
\[
v_{GS}\ge V_{tn}\qquad\text{and}\qquad v_{GD}\le V_{tn}.
\]
(The first inequality is inversion; the second is pinch-off of the drain end. Equality in the second is the boundary, which may equivalently be labelled triode.)

\[\boxed{(a)\ v_{GS}=0.50\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{DS}=4.00\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{GD}=-3.50\,\mathrm{V},\ \text{cutoff},\ i_D=0
} \]
\[\boxed{(b)\ v_{GS}=2.20\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{DS}=0.50\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{GD}=1.70\,\mathrm{V},\ \text{triode formula}
} \]
\[\boxed{(c)\ v_{GS}=2.20\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{DS}=3.30\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{GD}=-1.10\,\mathrm{V},\ \text{saturation formula}
} \]
\[\boxed{(d)\ v_{GS}=2.20\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{DS}=1.40\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{GD}=0.80\,\mathrm{V},\ \text{pinch-off (either formula)}
} \]
\[\boxed{(e)\ v_{GS}\ge V_{tn}\ \text{and}\ v_{GD}\le V_{tn}
} \]

