\[
k_n=(200\,\mu\mathrm{A}/\mathrm{V}^2)\cdot\frac{16.0}{0.80}=4.00\,\mathrm{mA}/\mathrm{V}^2.
\]

**(a)** \(v_{GS}=2.10-0.30=1.80\,\mathrm{V}\), \(v_{DS}=2.80-0.30=2.50\,\mathrm{V}\), \(v_{GD}=2.10-2.80=-0.70\,\mathrm{V}\), \(v_{OV}=1.80-0.60=1.20\,\mathrm{V}\).

**(b)** \(v_{GS}=1.80\,\mathrm{V}\ge 0.60\,\mathrm{V}\) and \(v_{DS}=2.50\,\mathrm{V}\ge 1.20\,\mathrm{V}\) (equivalently \(v_{GD}=-0.70\,\mathrm{V}\le 0.60\,\mathrm{V}\)): **saturation**.
\[
i_D=\tfrac12(4.00\,\mathrm{mA}/\mathrm{V}^2)(1.20\,\mathrm{V})^2=2.88\,\mathrm{mA}.
\]

**(c)** \(p=v_{DS}i_D=(2.50\,\mathrm{V})(2.88\,\mathrm{mA})=7.20\,\mathrm{mW}\).

**(d)** New source at \(2.80\,\mathrm{V}\), new drain at \(0.30\,\mathrm{V}\), body tied to the new source. Then \(v_{GS}'=2.10-2.80=-0.70\,\mathrm{V}<0.60\,\mathrm{V}\), so the relabelled device is in **cutoff**.

\[\boxed{(a)\ v_{GS}=1.80\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{DS}=2.50\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{GD}=-0.70\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{OV}=1.20\,\mathrm{V}
} \]
\[\boxed{(b)\ \text{saturation},\ i_D=2.88\,\mathrm{mA}
} \]
\[\boxed{(c)\ p=7.20\,\mathrm{mW}
} \]
\[\boxed{(d)\ \text{cutoff}
} \]

