ELEC:9924067.canonicalSolution:
**(a)**
\[
\begin{aligned}
v_{GS}&=3.40-5.00=-1.60\,\mathrm{V},&
v_{GD}&=3.40-1.80=+1.60\,\mathrm{V},\\
v_{SG}&=5.00-3.40=+1.60\,\mathrm{V},&
v_{SD}&=5.00-1.80=+3.20\,\mathrm{V},\\
v_{DG}&=1.80-3.40=-1.60\,\mathrm{V}.
\end{aligned}
\]

**(b)** Algebraic: \(v_{GS}=-1.60\,\mathrm{V}\le V_{tp}=-0.80\,\mathrm{V}\) (inverted) and \(v_{GD}=+1.60\,\mathrm{V}\ge -0.80\,\mathrm{V}\) (drain end pinched off) \(\Rightarrow\) **saturation**.

Source-referenced: \(v_{SG}=1.60\,\mathrm{V}\ge |V_{tp}|=0.80\,\mathrm{V}\) and \(v_{SD}=3.20\,\mathrm{V}\ge 1.60-0.80=0.80\,\mathrm{V}\) \(\Rightarrow\) **saturation**. The two tests agree.

**(c)** Overdrive \(v_{SG}-|V_{tp}|=0.80\,\mathrm{V}\),
\[
i_{SD}=\tfrac12(0.50\,\mathrm{mA}/\mathrm{V}^2)(0.80\,\mathrm{V})^2=0.160\,\mathrm{mA}.
\]

**(d)** \(i_{SD}\) leaves the drain, so the current **entering** the drain is \(-i_{SD}<0\) (negative).

\[\boxed{(a)\ v_{GS}=-1.60\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{GD}=+1.60\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{SG}=1.60\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{SD}=3.20\,\mathrm{V},\ v_{DG}=-1.60\,\mathrm{V}
} \]
\[\boxed{(b)\ \text{saturation (both tests)}
} \]
\[\boxed{(c)\ i_{SD}=0.160\,\mathrm{mA}
} \]
\[\boxed{(d)\ \text{current entering the drain is negative}
} \]

