ELEC:9924070.canonicalSolution:
\(v_{GS}=3.50\,\mathrm{V}>0.60\,\mathrm{V}\), so not cutoff. Overdrive \(v_{OV}=2.90\,\mathrm{V}\). Load: \(i_D=(5.00-v_D)/1.00\) with \(i_D\) in milliamperes and \(v_D\) in volts, i.e. \(i_D=5.00-v_D\).

**(a)** Saturation candidate:
\[
i_D=\tfrac12(2.00)(2.90)^2=8.41\,\mathrm{mA},\qquad v_D=5.00-8.41=-3.41\,\mathrm{V}.
\]
This \(v_D\) is negative (impossible for \(i_D\ge 0\) on this load line) and fails \(v_D\ge 2.90\,\mathrm{V}\). **Inconsistent.**

**(b)** Equate the triode law to the load line:
\[
2.00\bigl[(2.90)v_D-v_D^2/2\bigr]=5.00-v_D
\qquad\Rightarrow\qquad
v_D^2-6.80\,v_D+5.00=0.
\]
Discriminant \(46.24-20=26.24\), \(\sqrt{26.24}=5.1225\),
\[
v_D=\frac{6.80\pm 5.1225}{2}=5.96\,\mathrm{V}\quad\text{or}\quad 0.839\,\mathrm{V}.
\]

**(c)** The root \(5.96\,\mathrm{V}\) exceeds \(V_{DD}\) (negative resistor current) and lies outside the triode interval \(v_D<2.90\,\mathrm{V}\). The root \(0.839\,\mathrm{V}\) satisfies \(0\le 0.839<2.90\) and \(v_D\le V_{DD}\). Then \(i_D=5.00-0.839=4.16\,\mathrm{mA}\). Unique consistent solution: **triode**, \(i_D=4.16\,\mathrm{mA}\), \(v_D=0.839\,\mathrm{V}\).

**(d)** The triode \(i_D(v_{DS})\) is a downward-opening parabola; a straight load line can intersect it twice algebraically. Only the intersection that lies inside the defining interval \(0\le v_{DS}\le v_{OV}\) (and on the physical load segment \(0\le v_{DS}\le V_{DD}\)) is an operating point of the model.

\[\boxed{(a)\ i_D=8.41\,\mathrm{mA},\ v_D=-3.41\,\mathrm{V},\ \text{inconsistent}
} \]
\[\boxed{(b)\ v_D^2-6.80 v_D+5=0;\ \text{roots }5.96\,\mathrm{V},\ 0.839\,\mathrm{V}
} \]
\[\boxed{(c)\ \text{triode},\ i_D=4.16\,\mathrm{mA},\ v_D=0.839\,\mathrm{V}
} \]
\[\boxed{(d)\ \text{parabola–line intersection can lie outside the triode interval}
} \]

