ELEC:9924179.statement:
An NMOS common-source voltage amplifier is to be designed under a fixed current budget. \(V_{DD}=3.30\,\mathrm{V}\), \(I_D=0.200\,\mathrm{mA}\) exactly, \(\lambda=0\), \(V_{TN}=0.500\,\mathrm{V}\), \(k_n'=250\,\mu\mathrm{A/V^2}\). The source is at DC and AC ground, the only load is \(R_D\) to \(V_{DD}\), and the gate is driven by an ideal voltage. Use saturation square-law, \(g_m=2I_D/V_{OV}\), and \(A_v=-g_m R_D=-2I_D R_D/V_{OV}\). Allowed overdrives: \(V_{OV}\in\{0.200,0.250,0.300,0.400\}\,\mathrm{V}\). For each \(V_{OV}\), choose the smallest \(R_D\) from the continuum \(R_D>0\) that achieves \(\lvert A_v\rvert\ge 15.0\), then audit:
- saturation margin: \(V_{DS}-V_{OV}\ge 0.150\,\mathrm{V}\) at the quiescent point, with \(V_{DS}=V_{DD}-I_D R_D\);
- output common-mode floor: \(V_D\ge 1.00\,\mathrm{V}\);
- resistor bound: \(R_D\le 20.0\,\mathrm{k}\Omega\);
- device size: \(W/L=g_m/(k_n' V_{OV})\le 80.0\).

(a) For each allowed \(V_{OV}\), compute the minimum \(R_D\) meeting \(\lvert A_v\rvert=15.0\), the associated \(g_m\), \(W/L\), \(V_D\), \(V_{DS}-V_{OV}\), and a pass/fail on every audit.
(b) List every surviving \(V_{OV}\). Among survivors, select the design with the largest saturation margin \(V_{DS}-V_{OV}\).
(c) For the selected design, determine the available positive peak swing \(I_D R_D\) (onset of cutoff) and the available negative peak swing \(V_{DS}-V_{OV}\) (onset of triode). The usable linear peak \(\lvert v_o\rvert\) is the minimum of those two instantaneous bounds; do not subtract the quiescent \(0.150\,\mathrm{V}\) audit margin a second time. Report that peak and the corresponding peak \(\lvert v_{gs}\rvert\) from the linear gain.
(d) Explain, using only the table of (a), why increasing \(V_{OV}\) at fixed \(I_D\) forces a larger \(R_D\) to hold the gain and therefore threatens the drain-voltage floor, while decreasing \(V_{OV}\) increases \(W/L\) and \(g_m\). Identify the binding constraint that eliminates \(V_{OV}=0.400\,\mathrm{V}\).

ELEC:9924211.canonicalSolution:
The oxide and overlap products are geometry only; they do not yet require a region test.

**(a)**
\[
WLC_{\mathrm{ox}}'=50.0\times 1.00\times 3.45=172.5\,\mathrm{fF},\qquad
WC_{\mathrm{ov}}'=50.0\times 0.230=11.50\,\mathrm{fF}.
\]

**(b)** Overlap adds to \(C_{gs}\) and \(C_{gd}\) in every region. Junction values are given and bias-independent here.

Cutoff (channel absent): intrinsic gate charge sits on the body, so
\[
C_{gs}=11.50\,\mathrm{fF},\quad C_{gd}=11.50\,\mathrm{fF},\quad C_{gb}=172.5\,\mathrm{fF},\quad C_{sb}=18.0\,\mathrm{fF},\quad C_{db}=14.0\,\mathrm{fF}.
\]

Triode (inverted channel from source to drain, both ends inverted):
\[
C_{gs}=C_{gd}=\tfrac12(172.5)+11.50=97.75\,\mathrm{fF},\quad C_{gb}=0,\quad C_{sb}=18.0\,\mathrm{fF},\quad C_{db}=14.0\,\mathrm{fF}.
\]

Saturation (drain end pinched off; the stated model assigns two-thirds of the oxide to the source and none of the oxide to the drain):
\[
C_{gs}=\tfrac23(172.5)+11.50=126.5\,\mathrm{fF},\quad C_{gd}=11.50\,\mathrm{fF},\quad C_{gb}=0,\quad C_{sb}=18.0\,\mathrm{fF},\quad C_{db}=14.0\,\mathrm{fF}.
\]

**(c)** Source and body are both AC ground. In saturation:
- gate to AC ground: \(C_{gs}\) (and \(C_{gb}\), which is zero in this model);
- drain to AC ground: \(C_{db}\);
- bridge gate–drain: \(C_{gd}\).

\(C_{sb}\) has both terminals at AC ground, so it is shorted out of the small-signal network.

**(d)** Student value \(172.5\,\mathrm{fF}\) versus saturation \(C_{gs}=126.5\,\mathrm{fF}\):
\[
\frac{172.5-126.5}{126.5}=\frac{46.0}{126.5}=+0.364=+36.4\%.
\]
The error is positive (overestimate): dropping the two-thirds factor overstates the intrinsic piece by more than the omitted overlap understates it.

\[\boxed{(a)\ WLC_{\mathrm{ox}}'=172.5\,\mathrm{fF},\ WC_{\mathrm{ov}}'=11.50\,\mathrm{fF}
} \]
\[\boxed{(b)\ \text{cutoff: }C_{gs}=C_{gd}=11.50\,\mathrm{fF},\ C_{gb}=172.5\,\mathrm{fF},\ C_{sb}=18.0\,\mathrm{fF},\ C_{db}=14.0\,\mathrm{fF}
} \]
\[\boxed{\text{triode: }C_{gs}=C_{gd}=97.75\,\mathrm{fF},\ C_{gb}=0,\ C_{sb}=18.0\,\mathrm{fF},\ C_{db}=14.0\,\mathrm{fF}
} \]
\[\boxed{\text{sat: }C_{gs}=126.5\,\mathrm{fF},\ C_{gd}=11.50\,\mathrm{fF},\ C_{gb}=0,\ C_{sb}=18.0\,\mathrm{fF},\ C_{db}=14.0\,\mathrm{fF}
} \]
\[\boxed{(c)\ \text{gate: }C_{gs}\ (C_{gb}=0);\ \text{drain: }C_{db};\ \text{bridge: }C_{gd};\ C_{sb}\ \text{shorted}
} \]
\[\boxed{(d)\ +0.364\ (+36.4\%)
} \]

