ELEC:9924228.canonicalSolution:
Output-pole CS, \(v_{gs}=v_{s}\), \(r_{o}\to\infty\). Then \(\mathrm{GBW}=g_{m}/(2\pi C_{L})\) is independent of \(R_{D}\).

**(a)**
\[
\mathrm{GBW}=\frac{4.00\times 10^{-3}}{2\pi(6.00\times 10^{-12})}=106\,\mathrm{MHz}.
\]

**(b)** \(|A_{0}|=g_{m}R_{D}=25.0\) \(\Rightarrow\) \(R_{D}=25.0/4.00\,\mathrm{mS}=6.25\,\mathrm{k}\Omega\).
\[
f_{H}=\frac{\mathrm{GBW}}{25.0}=4.24\,\mathrm{MHz}.
\]

**(c)** The two inequalities require \(\mathrm{GBW}\ge 25.0\times 8.00\,\mathrm{MHz}=200\,\mathrm{MHz}\). Available GBW is only \(106\,\mathrm{MHz}\), so **no** \(R_{D}>0\) meets both constraints. Deficit: \(200-106=94\,\mathrm{MHz}\). Largest \(f_{H}\) at \(|A_{0}|=25.0\) is \(4.24\,\mathrm{MHz}\).

**(d)** Either doubling \(g_{m}\) at fixed \(C_{L}\) or halving \(C_{L}\) at fixed \(g_{m}\) doubles GBW to \(212\,\mathrm{MHz}>200\,\mathrm{MHz}\), so the specification of (c) **becomes feasible** in this model for each remedy.
Audit of (i): doubling \(W\) at fixed overdrive doubles \(C_{db}\) and \(C_{gd}\), both of which appear at the drain and therefore contribute to the effective \(C_{L}\). In a real layout \(C_{L}\) is **not** unchanged, and the GBW improvement is less than a factor of two.

\[\boxed{(a)\ \mathrm{GBW}=106\,\mathrm{MHz}
} \]
\[\boxed{(b)\ R_{D}=6.25\,\mathrm{k}\Omega,\ f_{H}=4.24\,\mathrm{MHz}
} \]
\[\boxed{(c)\ \text{no }R_{D}\ \text{meets both};\ \text{deficit }94\,\mathrm{MHz};\ \max f_{H}\text{ at }|A_{0}|=25\text{ is }4.24\,\mathrm{MHz}
} \]
\[\boxed{(d)\ \text{both remedies: new GBW}=212\,\mathrm{MHz},\ \text{feasible in the model};\ \text{(i) }C_{db},C_{gd}\propto W\text{ load the drain, so }C_{L}\text{ is not fixed}
} \]

