SIG:9926265.canonicalSolution:
(a) $A^k=0$ for every $k\ge 1$. Thus $\mathcal{C}(A,B)=[B\ 0]$ has rank $1$, and $\mathcal{R}=\operatorname{span}\{e_1\}$. A concrete unreachable state is $x_f=e_2=(0,1)^\mathrm{T}$ (or any state with nonzero second coordinate). From the origin, $x[N]=B u[N-1]=(u[N-1],0)^\mathrm{T}$ never leaves the first axis.

(b) For arbitrary $x[0]$, the update is $x[1]=(u[0],0)^\mathrm{T}$. Choosing $u[0]=0$ yields $x[1]=0$ in one step, independently of $x[0]$ (because $A=0$ annihilates the second coordinate). Every state is therefore controllable to the origin in one step, while the system is not completely reachable. When $A$ is singular, controllability to the origin does not imply reachability from the origin.

(c) $x_2[n+1]=0$ and $y[n]=x_2[n]$, so $y[0]=x_2[0]$ and $y[n]=0$ for all $n\ge 1$, independently of the input and of $x_1$. The pair $(A,C)$ is not observable ($\mathcal{O}$ has rank $1$): $x_1$ is invisible. The output is a one-step memory of the *initial second coordinate*.

(d) With $A'=\operatorname{diag}(0,1/2)$ one still has $\mathcal{R}=\operatorname{span}\{e_1\}$ (the second coordinate of a forced trajectory from the origin remains $0$). The system is not completely controllable to the origin: from $x[0]=(0,4)^\mathrm{T}$ one has $x_2[n]=4\cdot(1/2)^n$, which is never zero in finite time, and $u$ cannot affect $x_2$. The second coordinate decays geometrically by $1/2$ per step but remains nonzero for all finite $n$.

(e) $\mathcal{C}(A'',B'')=\bigl(\begin{smallmatrix}0&1\\ 1&0\end{smallmatrix}\bigr)$ has rank $2$, so the pair is completely reachable (and, $A''$ being nilpotent, also completely controllable to the origin). The dynamics are $x_1[n+1]=x_2[n]$, $x_2[n+1]=u[n]$, hence $x[2]=(u[0],u[1])^\mathrm{T}$. Deadbeat from $(5,-2)^\mathrm{T}$ to the origin: $u[0]=u[1]=0$. From the origin to $(1,0)^\mathrm{T}$: $u[0]=1$, $u[1]=0$.

\[
\boxed{(a)\ A^k=0\ (k\ge 1);\ \operatorname{rank}\mathcal{C}=1;\ \mathcal{R}=\operatorname{span}\{e_1\};\ e_2\ \mathrm{unreachable}
}
\]
\[
\boxed{(b)\ u[0]=0\ \mathrm{sends\ every\ }x[0]\ \mathrm{to\ }0\ \mathrm{in\ one\ step};\ \mathrm{CTO}\not\Rightarrow\mathrm{reachability\ when\ }A\ \mathrm{singular}
}
\]
\[
\boxed{(c)\ y[0]=x_2[0],\ y[n]=0\ (n\ge 1);\ \mathrm{not\ observable};\ \mathrm{memory\ of\ initial\ }x_2
}
\]
\[
\boxed{(d)\ \mathcal{R}=\operatorname{span}\{e_1\};\ \mathrm{not\ CTO};\ x_2[n]=4\cdot(1/2)^n\neq 0\ \mathrm{for\ all\ finite\ }n
}
\]
\[
\boxed{(e)\ \operatorname{rank}\mathcal{C}=2;\ \mathrm{completely\ reachable\ and\ CTO};\ u=(0,0)\ \mathrm{to\ origin};\ u=(1,0)\ \mathrm{origin}\to(1,0)^\mathrm{T}
}
\]

