(a) \(L=24/(s+3)\), \(T=24/(s+27)=8/(s/3+9)\), more simply \(T(s)=24/(s+27)\). Crossover: \(24/\sqrt{\omega^2+9}=1\) gives \(\omega_{\mathrm{gc}}=\sqrt{567}=23.8\,\mathrm{rad/s}\). Samples of \(|W_m T|\): \(0.267\), \(0.761\), \(0.707\), \(0.778\). Limit \(0\) because \(T\sim 24/s\). None of these values is \(\ge 1\), so the data do **not** refute \(\|W_m T\|_\infty<1\).

(b) At \(\omega=20.0\): \(|L|=1.19\) and \(1/|W_m|=1.01\), so \(|L|<1/|W_m|\) **fails**. At \(\omega=60.0\): \(|L|=0.400\) and \(1/|W_m|=0.469\), so the surrogate **holds**.

(c) \(|W_m T|<1\Leftrightarrow |W_m L/(1+L)|<1\Leftrightarrow |1+L|>|W_m|\,|L|\) wherever \(1+L\neq 0\). At \(\omega=20\) with \(K=8\): \(|1+L|=1.66>1.18=|W_m|\,|L|\), so the exact inequality **holds**. It does **not** agree with the surrogate of (b), which failed: the surrogate is conservative (it ignores the \(+1\) in \(1+L\)).

(d) For every finite \(K>0\), \(T(s)=3K/(s+3+3K)\sim 3K/s\to 0\) while \(W_m(\infty)=3\) is finite, so the product tends to \(0\). Next \(T(0)=K/(1+K)\in(0,1)\), and \(|W_m(0)T(0)|=0.300\cdot K/(1+K)<0.300<1\) for every \(K>0\). At \(\omega=6\),
\[
|T(\mathrm{j}6,K)|=\frac{K}{\sqrt{(K+1)^2+4}}\to 1\quad(K\to\infty),
\]
and \(|W_m(\mathrm{j}6)|=0.422\), so \(|W_m T|(\mathrm{j}6)\to 0.422<1\). The sample never reaches \(1\); the supremum of admissible \(K\) for this single sample is \(+\infty\), which is *not* smaller than \(K=8.00\).

(e) \(|W_m(\mathrm{j}\omega)|=1\) at the unique \(\omega_\star=20.2\,\mathrm{rad/s}\). The gain placing crossover there is \(K=\sqrt{\omega_\star^2+9}/3=6.82\). Then \(|T(\mathrm{j}\omega_\star)|=0.660\) and \(|W_m T|(\omega_\star)=0.660<1\). Placing crossover at \(\omega_\star\) is **not sufficient** for \(\|W_m T\|_\infty<1\): it constrains one frequency (and there \(|W_m|=1\) so the test reduces to \(|T|<1\), which is automatic if the loop is stable with \(M_T\) not too large), but the \(\mathrm{H}_\infty\) peak can occur elsewhere.

\[
\boxed{(a)\ T=24/(s+27),\ \omega_{\mathrm{gc}}=23.8;\ |W_m T|=(0.267,0.761,0.707,0.778);\ \lim=0;\ \text{does not refute}
}
\]
\[
\boxed{(b)\ \omega=20:\ |L|=1.19>1.01=1/|W_m|\text{ (fails)};\ \omega=60:\ 0.400<0.469\text{ (holds)}
}
\]
\[
\boxed{(c)\ \text{exact holds at }\omega=20\text{ (}|1+L|=1.66>1.18\text{); disagrees with surrogate}
}
\]
\[
\boxed{(d)\ \lim|W_m T|=0\ \forall K;\ |W_m(0)T(0)|<1\ \forall K;\ K_{\sup}=+\infty\text{ (not smaller than }8\text{)}
}
\]
\[
\boxed{(e)\ \omega_\star=20.2,\ K=6.82;\ |T|=0.660=|W_m T|;\ \text{not sufficient for }\|W_m T\|_\infty<1
}
\]

