The same \(F\) and \(Q\) as in Problem 57 are used. Recall the transformation rules under \(F^*=QF\): the second Piola–Kirchhoff stress must satisfy \(S^*=S\), the first Piola–Kirchhoff stress must satisfy \(P^*=QP\), and the Cauchy stress must satisfy \(\sigma^*=Q\sigma Q^{\mathrm{T}}\), with \(P=J\sigma F^{-\mathrm{T}}\) and \(S=F^{-1}P\) when \(J=\det F\). Four candidate constitutive assignments with \(\mu=175\,\mathrm{kPa}\) are proposed:
(i) \(S(F)=\mu(C-I)\), \(C=F^{\mathrm{T}}F\);
(ii) \(P(F)=\mu F\);
(iii) \(P(F)=\mu F^{\mathrm{T}}\);
(iv) \(\sigma(F)=\mu(U-I)\), where \(U=C^{1/2}\) is the right stretch (so \(F=RU\)).
For each candidate compute the stress at \(F\) and at \(F^*\), compute the appropriate objective transform of the stress at \(F\), and accept or reject the candidate by comparing those two tensors. For (i) also push \(S\) forward to Cauchy stress \(\sigma=J^{-1}FSF^{\mathrm{T}}\) at \(F\) and at \(F^*\) and verify that this pair does (or does not) transform as a spatial tensor. For (iv) compute \(R=FU^{-1}\) at both \(F\) and \(F^*\) (you may use that \(R^*=QR\)) and exhibit the mismatch or agreement explicitly.

FEM:9911085.statement:
A sequence of conforming piecewise-linear finite element solutions on uniformly refined meshes gives the following errors:
\[
\begin{array}{c|cccc}
h & 0.20 & 0.10 & 0.050 & 0.025\\ \hline
\|u-u_h\|_{H^1} & 8.10\times10^{-2} & 4.05\times10^{-2} & 2.03\times10^{-2} & 1.01\times10^{-2}\\
\|u-u_h\|_{L^2} & 6.40\times10^{-3} & 1.60\times10^{-3} & 4.00\times10^{-4} & 1.00\times10^{-4}
\end{array}
\]
For each consecutive pair of meshes, compute the observed order \(p=\log(E_h/E_{h/2})/\log 2\) in each norm. State the asymptotic order supported by each error sequence, and use that order together with the finest-mesh error to predict both errors at \(h=0.0125\).
